.TH wsblast-render 1  "wsblast-render 0.2.5" 
.SH NAME
wsblast\-render \- Render a saved JSON report (from \-\-format json) or comparison (from \-\-compare \-\-format json) as HTML, Markdown or text without running a test
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwsblast render\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREPORT.json\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render a saved JSON report (from \-\-format json) or comparison (from \-\-compare \-\-format json) as HTML, Markdown or text without running a test
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: html]
Format to render
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
html: Self\-contained HTML page with charts of the time series
.IP \(bu 2
markdown: GitHub Flavored Markdown
.IP \(bu 2
text: Terminal tables
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the rendered report to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIREPORT.json\fR>
JSON report written by `wsblast \-\-format json` (schema 1.x), or comparison written by `wsblast \-\-compare ... \-\-format json` (schema 1.1 or 1.2)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.5
